# Gentian OS installer non-secret configuration template
#
# Usage:
#   cp install.env.template install.env
#   edit install.env
#   ./install.sh
#
# Notes:
# - install.sh auto-loads ./install.env when present.
# - Values in this file are non-secret and may be committed only if your
#   organization allows it. Prefer environment-specific private copies.
# - Put secrets in install.secrets.env (MASTER_PASSWORD, registry, SMTP creds,
#   optional CF_API_TOKEN and GENTIAN_DEPLOYMENTS_GIT_TOKEN).

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cluster-scoped values moved to gentian-deployments
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Do not define cluster behavior values in install.env anymore.
# Configure these in:
#   clusters/<cluster>/kernel/cluster-settings.env   — hand-maintained runtime knobs
#   clusters/<cluster>/kernel/claims/cluster.yaml    — KERNEL_DOMAIN (the ONLY
#     place it's authored; install.sh reads/writes it here, never in
#     cluster-settings.env — see gentian-os/docs/deployment.md §1)
#   clusters/<cluster>/kernel/values.yaml            — cluster-unique Helm
#     overlay (image tag pin, cloudflare.zoneID/tunnelCNAME, etc.)
#   gentian-deployments/profiles/<stage>.yaml        — tier-wide policy shared
#     by every cluster of that stage (log level, ACME issuer, ...)
#
# Exception — first bootstrap only: a brand-new cluster's Claim doesn't exist
# until install.sh creates it, so KERNEL_DOMAIN has to come from somewhere
# the first time. Leave it unset and install.sh prompts for it interactively,
# or predefine it here to skip that prompt (e.g. for a non-interactive/CI
# run):
# KERNEL_DOMAIN=platform.example.com
# Once the Claim is scaffolded, this line stops mattering — install.sh reads
# from claims/cluster.yaml on every later run and never looks here again.
#
# Typical moved keys (cluster-settings.env, NOT KERNEL_DOMAIN — see above):
#   TENANCY_MODE, NETWORK_MODE, NODE_IP, MAIL_SERVICE_MODE,
#   SECRET_MODE, MINIO_ENDPOINT, CNPG_HOST, STORAGE_CLASS
#   TENANT_LIMITRANGE_DEFAULT_CPU, TENANT_LIMITRANGE_DEFAULT_MEMORY,
#   TENANT_LIMITRANGE_DEFAULT_REQUEST_CPU, TENANT_LIMITRANGE_DEFAULT_REQUEST_MEMORY,
#   TENANT_INITJOB_LIMIT_CPU, TENANT_INITJOB_LIMIT_MEMORY,
#   TENANT_INITJOB_REQUEST_CPU, TENANT_INITJOB_REQUEST_MEMORY
#   and (when MAIL_SERVICE_MODE=external):
#   EXTERNAL_SMTP_HOST, EXTERNAL_SMTP_PORT, EXTERNAL_SMTP_SSL, EXTERNAL_SMTP_STARTTLS
# Cloudflare split of responsibility:
#   - Secret token: CF_API_TOKEN (install.secrets.env)
#   - Optional verifier override: CF_ZONE_NAME (install.secrets.env)
#   - Operator runtime metadata: cloudflare.zoneID / cloudflare.tunnelCNAME in
#     clusters/<cluster>/kernel/values.yaml

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cluster infra bootstrap
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Set to 0 only if cert-manager, CloudNativePG, and Reloader are already managed
# in this cluster and should not be installed by install.sh.
INSTALL_CLUSTER_INFRA=1

# Tool install behavior
# SKIP_TOOLS=0

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# cert-manager / ACME (optional overrides)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These are optional because install.sh has sensible defaults:
# - LETSENCRYPT_EMAIL defaults to admin@${KERNEL_DOMAIN}
# - ACME_ENV defaults to production
# Override only when your environment requires non-default behavior.
# LETSENCRYPT_EMAIL=platform-admin@example.com
# ACME_ENV=staging   — dev only: Let's Encrypt staging API (untrusted certs;
#                      avoids production rate limits). Pair with
#                      tenantDNS01ClusterIssuer: letsencrypt-staging-dns01-cloudflare
#                      in gentian-deployments dev values. See multi-tenancy.md §3.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Edge routing (optional — prefer gentian-deployments clusters/<cluster>/kernel/values.yaml
# or profiles/<stage>.yaml)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ROUTING_MODE selects the edge stack installed by install.sh and consumed by
# the operator (Helm value routingMode → env ROUTING_MODE):
#   gateway — Envoy Gateway + Gateway API (required; install.sh Step 3c)
# ROUTING_MODE=gateway

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OpenBao / secret derivation
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OpenBao KV v2 mount path (default: secret).
# Must match spec.openbao.kvMount in the Cluster XR claim.
# KV_MOUNT=secret

# OpenBao CLI version auto-installed to ~/.local/bin when 'bao' is not on PATH.
# Must match the appVersion of the OpenBao Helm chart in kernel/bootstrap/openbao-application.yaml.
# OPENBAO_CLI_VERSION=v2.5.0

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local install-only overrides (optional)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Keep this file for installer behavior and source repository selection.
# Secrets always belong in install.secrets.env.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Repository sources (optional)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# App/deployment repository sources
GENTIAN_APPS_REPO=https://github.com/gentian-org/gentian-apps
GENTIAN_APPS_BRANCH=main
GENTIAN_DEPLOYMENTS_REPO=https://github.com/gentian-org/gentian-deployments
GENTIAN_DEPLOYMENTS_BRANCH=main
# Cluster-first deployments layout selector:
#   clusters/<GENTIAN_DEPLOYMENTS_CLUSTER>/kernel
#   clusters/<GENTIAN_DEPLOYMENTS_CLUSTER>/tenants/*
# No <stage> segment in the tenants path — a cluster has exactly one stage
# for its whole lifetime, so its own tree is already implicitly that stage.
# Environment mapping and promotion flows: gentian-os/docs/deployment.md
# If present, install/update also auto-load:
#   clusters/<GENTIAN_DEPLOYMENTS_CLUSTER>/kernel/cluster-settings.env
# Values loaded there should define cluster runtime behavior and endpoints.
GENTIAN_DEPLOYMENTS_CLUSTER=default-cluster
GENTIAN_DEPLOYMENTS_STAGE=dev
# GENTIAN_DEPLOYMENTS_PATH=${HOME}/.gentian/gentian-deployments
#
# In-cluster App Store install/uninstall pushes commits to gentian-deployments via
# the operator lifecycle API. Set GENTIAN_DEPLOYMENTS_GIT_TOKEN in install.secrets.env
# (install.sh creates gentian-deployments-git-credentials in gentian-system).
# Also enable appLifecycle.deployments in clusters/<cluster>/kernel/values.yaml.

# GitHub Actions secret upload targets (optional CI_BOT_PAT).
GITHUB_ACTIONS_OS_REPO=gentian-org/gentian-os
GITHUB_ACTIONS_UI_REPO=gentian-org/gentian-ui

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Stage 1 container images (CI / GHCR)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# install.sh pulls published images — it does not build operator/portal images locally.
# gentian-os CI tags: develop (branch), <short-sha> (commit) — see .github/workflows/ci.yaml
# GENTIAN_OS_IMAGE_TAG=develop
# GENTIAN_OS_IMAGE_PULL_POLICY=Always
# gentian-ui CI tags portal images similarly; set PORTAL_IMAGE_TAG to match gentian-ui develop.
# PORTAL_IMAGE_TAG=develop
# PORTAL_SKIP_IMAGE_BUILD=true

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LLM / GPU Serving Support
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LLM_SUPPORT enables the deployment of the LLM serving stack (vLLM, LocalAI,
# LiteLLM proxy, and upgrading Envoy Gateway to Envoy AI Gateway).
# LLM_SUPPORT=false

# GPU_ACCELERATION enables GPU acceleration for the LLM stack. If true, the
# installer validates that the cluster has nodes with allocatable GPUs and
# deploys vLLM backends. If false, the LLM stack runs in CPU-only mode
# (using LocalAI with GGUF models on CPU nodes).
# GPU_ACCELERATION=false

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Automation
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: set to 1 in CI to avoid interactive prompts
GENTIAN_NONINTERACTIVE=0
